    static let trifle = "Nespresso Hazelnut Coffee And Chocolate Trifle Recipe\nAverage Calories Per Serving: 1100 Kcal \n\nServes:\n10\n\nCooking Time:\n40-60 Minutes\nAbout This Recipe\nChocolate lovers, this one’s for you. This Hazelnut Coffee & Chocolate Trifle layers soft homemade chocolate cake with rich chocolate custard and hazelnut coffee cream made with LANCEWOOD® Mascarpone. Finished with toasted hazelnuts, it’s a chocolate trifle recipe made for sharing. \n\nIngredients:\nChocolate Cake \n125g butter (½ cup) \n180g white sugar \n2 large eggs \n5ml vanilla extract (1 tsp) \n180g flour \nA pinch of salt \n10ml baking powder (2 tsp) \n30g cocoa powder \n225ml milk \n \nChocolate Custard \n1.5 litres full cream milk \n100g cornflour \n55g cocoa powder \n¼ tsp salt \n180g castor sugar \n150g dark chocolate \n2 tsp vanilla extract \n \nHazelnut Coffee Cream \n500g Lancewood mascarpone \n750ml cream \n80g icing sugar \n100ml Nespresso Hazelnut Brownie coffee \n \nCoffee Syrup \n200ml Nespresso Hazelnut Brownie coffee \n40g castor sugar \n \nTo Garnish \n30g chopped toasted hazelnuts \nGrated chocolate \n\nMethod\nChocolate Cake \n    1    Preheat the oven to 190°C. Grease and line two 20cm diameter cake tins.\n    2    Cream the butter and sugar together using an electric or stand mixer for about 5 minutes, until very light and fluffy. \n    3    Add the eggs, one at a time, beating well after each addition. Add the vanilla extract. Scrape down the sides of the bowl and mix well. \n    4    Sift all the dry ingredients together in a separate bowl. \n    5    Add the dry ingredients to the creamed mixture alternately with the milk, beating well between each addition. \n    6    Divide the mixture between the prepared cake tins, smoothing the mixture evenly with a spatula. \n    7    Bake for 25–30 minutes, or until a skewer inserted into the centre comes out clean. \n    8    Cool in the tins for 5–10 minutes, then turn out and allow to cool completely on cooling racks. \n \nChocolate Custard \n    1    Combine the cornflour, cocoa powder, castor sugar and salt in a bowl. Add 300ml of the milk and mix well to form a smooth paste. \n    2    Heat the remaining milk in a saucepan until it just starts to boil. \n    3    Gradually add the cornflour mixture to the hot milk, whisking constantly. \n    4    Continue cooking over medium heat, stirring continuously, until the mixture thickens and starts to bubble. \n    5    Remove from the heat. Add the vanilla extract and dark chocolate, stirring until the chocolate has completely melted and the mixture is smooth and combined.\n    6    Transfer to a bowl and cover with cling film, pressing it directly onto the surface of the custard to prevent a skin from forming.\n    7    Allow to cool to room temperature, then refrigerate until needed.\n   \nHazelnut Coffee Cream \n    1    Add the Lancewood mascarpone, cooled Nespresso coffee and icing sugar to a bowl. Whisk until smooth, taking care not to overmix. \n    2    In a separate bowl, whisk the cream to medium peaks. \n    3    Gently fold the whipped cream into the coffee mascarpone mixture until combined. \n \nCoffee Syrup \n    1    Combine the Nespresso coffee and castor sugar, stirring until the sugar has dissolved. \n    2    Set aside to cool. \n \nAssembly \n    1    Place one of the chocolate cakes at the bottom of a trifle dish.\n    2    Brush generously with the coffee syrup. \n    3    Spoon over approximately half of the chocolate custard, followed by half of the hazelnut coffee cream. \n    4    Repeat the layers with the remaining cake, coffee syrup, chocolate custardand hazelnut coffee cream. \n    5    Refrigerate for 1–2 hours, or until ready to serve. \n    6    Finish by piping some of the hazelnut coffee cream over the top. \n    7    Sprinkle with chopped toasted hazelnuts and grated chocolate."
